{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "The sunlight felt…different. Sharper, somehow. Arthur blinked, the familiar fuzziness of sleep receding to reveal a world rendered with unnerving detail. The grass was impossibly green, the sky a flawless azure, and the air hummed with a low, almost palpable energy. He sat up, a jolt of disorientation hitting him. His clothes – a worn flannel shirt and jeans – felt strangely…textured, almost like a high-resolution fabric. He glanced down and noticed his hands weren't his own. They were slightly larger, with subtly exaggerated knuckles and a faint, almost pixelated sheen to the skin. A nearby wooden fence, impossibly detailed with individual planks and weathered grain, seemed to ripple slightly, as if viewed through a low-resolution display. A digital bird chirped overhead, its song perfectly synthesized, yet somehow…real. Panic began to claw at his throat.\n\n***\n\nHe stood, legs unsteady, and took a hesitant step. The ground felt solid, yet strangely responsive to his weight. He looked around, and the landscape unfolded before him: rolling hills dotted with quaint, thatched-roof cottages, a winding river reflecting the impossibly blue sky. A path, perfectly paved and unnervingly straight, beckoned him forward.  He tried to call out, but his voice came out as a synthesized, slightly echoing tone.  A small, furry creature with oversized ears and bright, inquisitive eyes peeked out from behind a flower, its movements jerky and unnatural.  Arthur realized, with a chilling certainty, that this wasn’t reality. This wasn’t a dream. He was inside a video game, and he had absolutely no idea how to get out.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6729406118392944}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logprob": -0.9427294135093689}, {"token": "▁felt", "logprob": -0.1230592280626297}, {"token": "…", "logprob": -0.02061885967850685}, {"token": "different", "logpro